  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.3. Increased institutional capacity of labour administrations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Mongolian Parliament adopted a new Labour Law in July 2021. Among the reforms introduced, the new Labour Law empowers labour inspectors for the first time to carry out inspection visits without prior notice, as set out in Article 12(1)(a) of the ILO&#x2019;s Labour Inspection Convention, 1947 (No. 81).

In addition, Mongolia&#x2019;s General Agency for Specialized Inspection (GASI) revised its 5-year plan, in addition to the development of a strategic compliance plan. The introduction of this provision on unannounced labour inspection visits in the new Labour Law was the result of a recommendation from the ILO&#x2019;s 2016 labour inspection needs assessment, which measured the country&#x2019;s labour inspection law and practice against ILO Conventions No. 81 and No. 129. The ILO shared and discussed this and other recommendations with the tripartite partners in subsequent dialogues on the ratification of Conventions 81 and 129, leading to the eventual revision of this provision in the Labour Law in 2021.

With support from a European Union (EU), the ILO also supported the review of GASI&#x2019;s 5-year plan including providing technical feedback.</narrative>
   </description>
